/**
 * Every Material Symbol PadStudio ships, as drawable ids: `res/drawable/sym_<slot>.xml` (outline) and
 * `sym_<slot>_fill.xml` (filled), generated by `tools/lib/fetch_symbols.py` from Material Symbols Rounded at
 * google/material-design-icons@49d4db35 (Apache-2.0). The slot names and the Material name behind each are
 * in `docs/redesign/assets/symbols/map.json`; a property here is the slot in camelCase (`open_camera` →
 * [openCamera]), and its filled twin adds `Fill` ([openCameraFill]).
 *
 * Draw one with `SymIcon(Sym.today, contentDescription = null)` (ui/components) or
 * `Icon(painterResource(Sym.today), …)`. The drawables are white; Icon tints them with the content colour.
 *
 * Filled means selected or active (BRIEF). Use [filledIf] for that, but never let fill be the only sign of
 * selection: 23 of the 66 symbols look exactly the same filled and outlined (see
 * [fillLooksDifferent]), among them the Home and Setup rail icons. Pair it with a container, a colour
 * change and the selected semantics.
 */
